  "published": "2025-08-30T10:52:32.393Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "📦 Release Notes – V1.0.3\n\n🚀 New Features\n\nOptional Transaction Support (transactionOn)\n\nAdded transactionOn flag to all DapperExecutor methods (ExecuteAsync, ExecuteScalarAsync, QueryAsync, QueryFirstOrDefaultAsync, QueryMultipleAsync).\n\nWhen set to true, the operation executes inside a database transaction.\n\nOn success → transaction is automatically committed.\n\nOn failure → transaction is automatically rolled back.\n\nWhen set to false (default), the operation executes without a transaction.\n\n✅ Benefits\n\nSimplifies transaction management for developers.\n\nEnsures multiple operations succeed or fail together.\n\nReduces boilerplate transaction handling code.\n\nCompatible with SQL Server, MySQL (InnoDB), and PostgreSQL, and If any statement fails, the whole operation is rolled back automatically.",
